import Prim "mo:⛔";

// Candid record decoding: the field-skip count must be read at full width.
//
// `find_field` / `skip_fields` in rts/motoko-rts/src/idl.rs read the number of
// remaining record fields through the count slot that `with_record_typ` sets up.
// While that pointer was typed `*mut u8` the count was effectively taken modulo
// 256: a record whose number of trailing extra fields is an exact multiple of
// 256 produced a skip count of 0, so the decoder skipped none of them and left
// the data pointer stranded mid-record.
//
// The blob below is a single record { a : Blob } carrying 256 trailing extra
// fields (each a nat with a value, i.e. not zero-width). Extra fields are valid
// under Candid subtyping, so decoding it at the subtype ?{ a : Blob } must skip
// all 256 and succeed. With the `*mut u8` count, 256 mod 256 = 0 skipped none of
// them, leaving the 256 field values unconsumed, and the decode failed with a
// "left-over bytes" trap. Reading the count as `*mut u32` skips all 256 and the
// record decodes cleanly.
//
// This test guards that fix: on a regression the decode traps here instead of
// binding `rec`. `from_candid` is unimplemented in the interpreter (FromCandidE),
// so only the compiled backend is exercised.

let b : Blob = Prim.arrayToBlob([
    68,73,68,76,2,109,123,108,129,2,97,0,208,15,125,209,
    15,125,210,15,125,211,15,125,212,15,125,213,15,125,214,15,
